{"id":1342,"date":"2020-11-26T18:45:42","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T02:45:42","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1342"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:49","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:49","slug":"program-the-turret-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-turret-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Program the Turret Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162fedf08\" name=\"6a22162fedf08\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What it does<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The Turret Bot is controlled with the Smart Inventor Board&#8217;s IR sensors. The right and left sensors will move the Turret Bot in those directions and the center IR sensor is used for firing the rubber band.<\/p>\n<p>This is the turret bot&#8217;s pseudocode:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check the left, center, and right sensors.<\/li>\n<li>If the right sensor senses an object, swing to the right.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if the left sensor senses an object, swing to the left.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if the center sensor senses an object, shoot the rubber band.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162fee03b\" name=\"6a22162fee03b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The first thing you need to do in your code is set up the Smart Inventor library. Since your motors will be controlling the turret, you need to include those in void setup().<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162fee0b5\" name=\"6a22162fee0b5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add IR sensors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your IR sensors are super important for this robot! The first thing you need to do is check the base levels that each sensor is reading. This will help you tell if the sensors are detecting something nearby.<\/p>\n<p>In void setup(), you&#8217;ll be reading the sensors&#8217; values, which you&#8217;re going to save in some variables. Not even IR sensors are perfect, so subtract 50 from each of the sensors to create a buffer.<\/p>\n<p>You may or may not have realized this: your Smart Inventor Board is upside down! For the Turret Bot, the right sensor is pin 19 and the left sensor is pin 21.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint baseLevelLeft;\r\nint baseLevelCenter;\r\nint baseLevelRight;\r\n\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n \r\n  baseLevelLeft = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n  baseLevelCenter = analogRead(20) - 50;\r\n  baseLevelRight = analogRead(19) - 50;\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162fee118\" name=\"6a22162fee118\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Read the sensors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In void loop(), include code that will read the sensors and check if they detect anything nearby. The good thing about using if, else if, and else statements for this part of the code is that each sensor will be checked one at a time, which will prevent your Turret Bot from just wiggling back and forth!<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n  \/\/ check sensors\r\n  int leftSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n  int centerSensor = analogRead(20);\r\n  int rightSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n \r\n  \/\/if right, turn right\r\n  if(rightSensor &lt; baseLevelRight)\r\n  {\r\n \r\n  }\r\n  \/\/ if left, turn left\r\n  else if(leftSensor &lt; baseLevelLeft)\r\n  {\r\n \r\n  }\r\n  \/\/ if center, shoot\r\n  else if(centerSensor &lt; baseLevelCenter)\r\n  {\r\n \r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162fee175\" name=\"6a22162fee175\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add motors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next, add your motors to void loop(). Your motors are going to move in small increments, so they&#8217;ll turn and stop for small amounts of time. This means you&#8217;ll have better control of your motors, which also means better control of shooting rubber bands!<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n  \/\/ check sensors\r\n  int leftSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n  int centerSensor = analogRead(20);\r\n  int rightSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n \r\n  \/\/if right, turn right\r\n  if(rightSensor &lt; baseLevelRight)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/move right\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 100);\r\n    delay(6);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, STOP, 0);\r\n    delay(2);\r\n  }\r\n  \/\/ if left, turn left\r\n  else if(leftSensor &lt; baseLevelLeft)\r\n  {    \r\n    \/\/ move left\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 100);\r\n    delay(6);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, STOP, 0);\r\n    delay(2);\r\n  }\r\n  \/\/ if center, shoot\r\n  else if(centerSensor &lt; baseLevelCenter)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ shoot\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 100);\r\n    delay(300);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, STOP, 0);\r\n    delay(100);\r\n  }\r\n \r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162fee1d6\" name=\"6a22162fee1d6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program LEDs<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You can also program your LEDs so they can give you extra feedback on what exactly your Turret Bot is doing. The two left LEDs will be on when the left sensor is covered, the two right LEDs will be on when the right sensor is covered, and the two middle LEDs will be on when the middle sensor is covered.<\/p>\n<p>The first thing you need to do is set up the LEDs as outputs. You can do this in void setup() with pinMode(). In void loop(), use digitalWrite() with pairs of LEDs so they turn on and off with certain sensors. These will be within the if, else if, and else statements that you already wrote.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n \r\nint baseLevelLeft;\r\nint baseLevelCenter;\r\nint baseLevelRight;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n \r\n  baseLevelLeft = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n  baseLevelCenter = analogRead(20) - 50;\r\n  baseLevelRight = analogRead(19) - 50;\r\n \r\n  pinMode(11, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(12, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(14, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(15, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(17, OUTPUT);\r\n  pinMode(18, OUTPUT);\r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {\r\n  \/\/ check sensors\r\n  int leftSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n  int centerSensor = analogRead(20);\r\n  int rightSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n \r\n  \/\/if right, turn right\r\n  if(rightSensor &lt; baseLevelRight)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ Right LEDs on\r\n    digitalWrite(11, HIGH);\r\n    digitalWrite(12, HIGH);\r\n \r\n    \/\/move right\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 100);\r\n    delay(6);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, STOP, 0);\r\n    delay(2);\r\n \r\n    \/\/ Right LEDs off\r\n    digitalWrite(11, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n  }\r\n  \/\/ if left, turn left\r\n  else if(leftSensor &lt; baseLevelLeft)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ left LEDs on\r\n    digitalWrite(17, HIGH);\r\n    digitalWrite(18, HIGH);\r\n \r\n    \/\/ move left\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 100);\r\n    delay(6);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, STOP, 0);\r\n    delay(2);\r\n \r\n    \/\/ left LEDs off\r\n    digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(18, LOW);\r\n  }\r\n  \/\/ if center, shoot\r\n  else if(centerSensor &lt; baseLevelCenter)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ center LEDs on\r\n    digitalWrite(14, HIGH);\r\n    digitalWrite(15, HIGH);\r\n \r\n    \/\/ shoot\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 100);\r\n    delay(300);\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, STOP, 0);\r\n    delay(100);\r\n \r\n    \/\/ center LEDs off\r\n    digitalWrite(14, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(15, LOW);\r\n  }\r\n \r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162fee230\" name=\"6a22162fee230\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your final code should look something like the one below.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt; \r\n\r\nint baseLevelLeft;\r\nint baseLevelCenter;\r\nint baseLevelRight; \r\n\r\nvoid setup() {  \r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();  \r\n \r\n    baseLevelLeft = analogRead(21) - 50;  \r\n    baseLevelCenter = analogRead(20) - 50;  \r\n    baseLevelRight = analogRead(19) - 50;   \r\n\r\n    pinMode(11, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(12, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(14, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(15, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(17, OUTPUT);  \r\n    pinMode(18, OUTPUT);\r\n} \r\n\r\nvoid loop() {  \r\n    \/\/ check sensors  \r\n    int leftSensor = analogRead(21);  \r\n    int centerSensor = analogRead(20);  \r\n    int rightSensor = analogRead(19);   \r\n\r\n    \/\/if right, turn right  \r\n    if(rightSensor &lt; baseLevelRight)  \r\n    {    \r\n        \/\/ Right LEDs on    \r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH);    \r\n        digitalWrite(12, HIGH);     \r\n\r\n        \/\/move right    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 100);    \r\n        delay(6);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, STOP, 0);    \r\n        delay(2);     \r\n\r\n        \/\/ Right LEDs off    \r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW);    \r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);  \r\n    }  \r\n\r\n    \/\/ if left, turn left  \r\n    else if(leftSensor &lt; baseLevelLeft)  \r\n    {    \r\n        \/\/ left LEDs on    \r\n        digitalWrite(17, HIGH);    \r\n        digitalWrite(18, HIGH);     \r\n\r\n        \/\/ move left    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 100);    \r\n        delay(6);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, STOP, 0);    \r\n        delay(2);     \r\n\r\n        \/\/ left LEDs off    \r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);    \r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);  \r\n    }  \r\n\r\n    \/\/ if center, shoot  \r\n    else if(centerSensor &lt; baseLevelCenter)  \r\n    {    \r\n        \/\/ center LEDs on    \r\n        digitalWrite(14, HIGH);    \r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);     \r\n\r\n        \/\/ shoot    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 100);    \r\n        delay(300);    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, STOP, 0);    \r\n        delay(100);     \r\n\r\n        \/\/ center LEDs off    \r\n        digitalWrite(14, LOW);    \r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);  \r\n    } \r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22162fee27b\" name=\"6a22162fee27b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Still not sure about this lesson or want to check your program? Watch the video![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=Wh_NwfdQaUs&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 What it does [vc_column_text]The Turret Bot is controlled with the Smart Inventor Board's IR sensors. The right and left sensors will move the Turret Bot in those&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-turret-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1746,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":true,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1777,1808,1793,1913,1910,1915,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2163,2216,2122,2171,2189,2197],"class_list":["post-1342","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-leds","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-sensors","lesson-tag-turret","module-turret","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1342","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1342\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1522,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1342\/revisions\/1522"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1746"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1342"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1342"},{"taxonomy":"lesso